{"file_path":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/defect_cocycle_with_findings.tex","new_string":"\\end{center}\n\n\\section*{Which operator powers H23a}\n\\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Which operator powers H23a}\n\nThe proof of \\cref{app:quad} forces a choice of operator, and it resolves\ncleanly in favour of the \\textbf{faithful skew product (\\texttt{sync})}, on a\n\\emph{coboundary-quotiented} character family. The reasoning:\n\n\\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=1.6em]\n\\item \\textbf{Faithfulness is non-negotiable for an inverse argument.} H23a runs\n\\emph{backwards}: a persistent $|W_n(x;\\chi,s)|$ must force a near-peripheral\neigenstate. That implication is valid only if the operator's spectral radius\n\\emph{is} the growth rate of $W_n$. Along the real orbit a single valuation\n$b_i$ drives both the residue step and the tilt weight $2^{s\\Delta_{b_i}}$, which\nis exactly the \\texttt{sync} coupling. The \\texttt{factored} operator draws an\nindependent valuation for the height, so its spectral radius does \\emph{not}\ngovern $W_n$.\n\n\\item \\textbf{The \\texttt{factored} gap is a mirage.} By \\cref{cor:run},\n$W_n(x;\\chi_2,0)=\\frac1n\\sum(-1)^{b_{i-1}}\\to \\E[(-1)^b]=-\\tfrac13$ (confirmed:\nmean $-0.353$ over $3.2\\times10^4$ orbits). The $\\chi_2$ component \\emph{does not\ndecay}. The \\texttt{factored} operator reports a gap there ($\\rho<\\rho_0$),\npredicting decay that does not occur---a false negative that would let a genuine\nnon-decaying sector through. \\texttt{sync} correctly returns\n$\\rho(\\Lcal_{\\chi_2})=\\rho(\\Lcal_{\\mathbf1})$ (no decay), matching reality.\n\n\\item \\textbf{The lone ungapped sector is not an obstruction---it is the\nreference.} $\\chi_2$ is a coboundary (\\cref{thm:cobound}); its Weyl sum is\nslaved to the valuation statistics, i.e.\\ to the $\\chi=\\mathbf1$ (height/pressure)\ndata. Equivalently, the orbit's residues are \\emph{not} uniform mod $3$: they sit\nat $1:2$ ratio $\\tfrac13:\\tfrac23$, the pushforward of the valuation parity. So\nthe correct annealed residue reference is this non-uniform law, and $\\chi_2$\ncarries no information beyond it. H23a must be posed on the quotient\n$\\widehat{\\Om_Q}/\\langle\\text{coboundaries}\\rangle$, where $\\chi_2$ is absorbed\ninto the reference.\n\n\\item \\textbf{On that quotient, \\texttt{sync} has a positive, $Q$-uniform gap.}\nExcluding $\\chi_2$, the worst character sits at fixed frequency $\\xi=1/6$ with\ngap ratio $0.9069$ for every $Q\\in\\{9,27,81\\}$ and both tilts, i.e.\n\\[\n\\kappa_Q^{\\text{(sync, non-coboundary)}}\\;=\\;0.0931,\\quad\\text{tilt-independent and $Q$-stable.}\n\\]\nThis is smaller than the pure residue gap $0.236$ (the height-survival mode lifts\nevery sector toward $1$), but it is bounded away from $0$---comfortably\n$\\gtrsim 1/\\mathrm{polylog}(Q)$, which is all H23a needs.\n\\end{enumerate}\n\n\\begin{keystatement}\n\\textbf{Decision.} Run H23a on the faithful \\texttt{sync} skew-product operator,\nrelative to the valuation-pushforward residue reference, restricting the\ncharacter family to the coboundary-quotient. There the finite gap is\n$\\kappa_Q\\approx0.093$, uniform in $Q$ and $s$. The \\texttt{factored} and\nresidue-only operators are kept as \\emph{diagnostics}: they isolate the pure\nresidue decorrelation ($\\kappa=1-\\tfrac{2^{1+s}-1}{2^{1+s}+1}$, stabilising at\n$0.236/0.074$) and certify that $\\chi_2$ is the unique difference between the two.\n\\end{keystatement}\n\n\\paragraph{Immediate follow-ups.}\n(1)~With the operator question settled, the open analytic task is to establish\nthe H23a gap $\\kappa_Q\\gtrsim1/\\mathrm{polylog}(Q)$ for the \\texttt{sync}\noperator on the coboundary-quotient at \\emph{all} $Q$ (numerically $\\approx0.093$\nand flat for $Q\\le3^4$; confirm to larger $Q$ and prove). (2)~Switch the\ndefect-window","old_string":"\\end{center}\n\n\\paragraph{Immediate follow-ups.}\n(1)~The residue-only uniform gap is computed over the full group to $Q=3^7$ and\nstabilizes; the \\texttt{factored} height coupling lets the killed operator\ninherit it; and the skew-product quadratic-character coboundary is now\n\\emph{proved} (\\cref{app:quad}). The remaining choice is which operator (faithful\nskew product vs.\\ factored) is the right vehicle for the H23a argument.\n(2)~Switch the defect-window","replace_all":false}